# ADR-002: Guest User Persistence

## Decision

Guest users are stored as regular User records, just like Google-authenticated users.

## Context

The app need to support guest login while allowing guests to create and manage tasks.

For guest login feature there are few options two of them are:

1. Store guest user only in local storage
2. Store guest user as actual user in DB

## Reason

- The main reason for choosing option 2 is that otherwise we would have two separate data flows based on the user's login type.

- For guest user fetching logic will be in frontend and for google authenticated user logic will be in backend which is not a good architecture.

- Also, storing the guests in DB allows thier tasks to persist across browser sessions as long as their authentication state is retained.

## Note

Guest accounts are not recoverable across devices because they don't have a permanent identity such as a Google account.
